<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vologases VI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vologases VI was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> who reigned from about 208 to 228 CE. He spent most of his reign disputing the throne with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artabanus-iv">Artabanus IV</a>, who controlled much of the empire, while Vologases held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and issued coins at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucia">Seleucia</a>. The rivalry weakened the Arsacids as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a> rose in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persis">Persis</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vologases-vi.jpg" alt="Vologases VI" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Vologases_VI_of_Parthia_(cropped),_Ecbatana_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
